Launch UAT agent to include {{.id}} in the UAT documentation.

CODEX RED-TEAM ASSESSMENT (Phase 3):
- This phase is MANDATORY. If codex fails or is skipped, verdict = "Insufficient Evidence".
- Run independent codex cross-check of the full implementation against the spec and PRD.
- Codex findings OVERRIDE the UAT agent's own assessment — codex is the tiebreaker.
- The UAT agent must NOT auto-complete the task; user approval is always required.

E2E WIRING VERIFICATION TABLE:
- Include a table in the UAT report with columns: Component | Entry Point Call Chain | Verified (Y/N)
- Every new component/function must have a verified call chain from the application entry point.
- Any row with Verified = N is a blocking finding.

VERDICTS:
- "Approved" — codex red-team passed, E2E wiring verified, user approved
- "Insufficient Evidence" — codex red-team was skipped, failed to run, or inconclusive
- "Rejected" — codex or UAT agent found spec gaps, wiring failures, or user rejected
